title: fantasy_trail_keeper
---
Mara: The stones are still firm along the ridge. When the wind comes up, wait in the old shelter.
Mara: I used to bring Dennis his mail. The climb took him ten minutes less than it took anybody else.
===

title: fantasy_wayfarer
---
Anwen: I'm taking two wheels of cheese to Brackenford. One of them may still be whole when I get there.
Anwen: The road down is easy to miss in cloud. Follow it past the first stand of pines.
===

title: fantasy_broker
---
Nell: Boot leather and lamp oil today. Have you come from the valley? I need to know if the trader still has any batteries.
Nell: A peddler sold me a thing that counts steps. The miller tied it to his wheel. It says the miller has walked to the coast three times.
===

title: fantasy_cooper
---
Tom: If you hear knocking, it's me putting hoops on a barrel. If you hear a bell, that's the goat in the old watch.
Tom: If he gets at that stack of hoops again, call me. I've only just got them in order.
===

title: fantasy_knight
---
Sir Cumference: I came from Math Town. I carry packages over the pass, or go up after anyone who's got themselves lost.
Sir Cumference: The wizard and I have been comparing spells. He gets quite cross when I ask to see his derivation.
===
